.TH FL-DOCS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-docs \- document viewer for PDF, EPUB, OpenDocument text, Markdown and comic books
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-docs\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
\fBfl-docs \-\-info\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-find\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.br
\fBfl-docs \-\-to\-pdf\fR \fIFILE\fR \fIOUT.pdf\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows PDF documents (through poppler), EPUB e-books, OpenDocument text
documents (.odt, .ott), Markdown (.md, .markdown) and comic books (.cbz, also .cbr, .cb7 and .cbt) in one
continuously scrolling strip of pages, with page thumbnails on the left.
.PP
E-books and OpenDocument text are laid out into pages by fl-docs itself:
headings, paragraphs with their alignment and indents, bold, italic and the
like, lists, simple tables, images and page breaks are kept; style sheets,
fonts embedded in the document and floating frames are not, so lines and
pages break differently than in the program that wrote the document. E-books
use 6 x 9 inch pages and start every chapter on a new page; OpenDocument text
uses the document's page size and margins. Markdown (CommonMark, with
GitHub's tables, strike-through and task lists) is laid out on A4 pages; its
title is the front matter's title or the first heading, and its images are
read from the disk next to the file (images on the web are left out).
E-books protected by DRM cannot
be shown. Comic books show their pictures (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, SVG) in the
natural order of their names, one per page. The zoom fits the width (of the
widest page) or the whole page, or is set from 10% to 800%. Search finds a
text on all pages, without regard to case, and highlights every match.
Printing goes to a CUPS printer with copies, a page range and two-sided
printing; e-books, OpenDocument text, Markdown and comic books are printed as fl-docs
lays them out. PDF documents protected by a password ask for it. A document
dropped onto the window opens.
.SH KEYS
.TP
Ctrl+O, Ctrl+P
Open, print.
.TP
Ctrl+F, Enter, F3, Shift+F3
Find; the next and the previous match.
.TP
Page Up, Page Down, Space, arrows, Home, End, N, P
Scroll; first and last page; next and previous page.
.TP
Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus, Ctrl+0, Ctrl+wheel
Zoom in, out, to 100%.
.TP
F9
Show or hide the thumbnails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR
Open at page \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-info\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-find\fR \fITEXT\fR]
Print the number of pages, the title and the page sizes in points and, with
\fB\-\-find\fR, every match as "hit PAGE X Y WIDTH HEIGHT" (points from the
top left corner), without opening a window.
.TP
\fB\-\-to\-pdf\fR \fIFILE\fR \fIOUT.pdf\fR
Write the PDF that printing would send: for an e-book, OpenDocument text or
comic book the pages as fl-docs lays them out, for a PDF a copy.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-printers\fR(1), \fBfl-view\fR(1)
